In the Early Access version of V Rising, Blood Rage originally had a cooldown of  and the following effect:
{{Quote|Shield self and nearby allies for  of your spell power and increase attack speed by  for .|width=5px}}

In the Gloomrot update the spell was then reworked into its current iteration.

In the Early Access version of V Rising Blood Fountain originally belonged to the Unholy Magic School under the name . It had a cooldown of  and the following effect:
{{Quote|Call down a pillar of energy that slows enemies in an area for  and heals allies for  of your spell power. After  the pillar erupts in a powerful burst of energy dealing  magic damage to enemies and healing allies for  of your spell power.|width=5px}}


It was reworked into its current iteration and moved to the Blood Magic School with the Secrets of Gloomrot update on May 17th, 2023.

Chaos Barrier was much different in the Early Access version of V Rising, as it launched a chaos bolt for each attack blocked. It had a cooldown of  and the following effect:
{{Quote|Increase movement speed by  and block melee and projectile attacks in front of you for . Blocking an attack launches a projectile towards the attacker dealing  damage, pushing the target towards you and inflicting Chaos Burn.|width=5px}}


During V Rising's first expansion, Secrets of Gloomrot, on May 17th, 2023 it received major changes. A new recast functionality was added.
It had a cooldown of  and the following effect:
{{Quote|Block melee and projectile attacks in front of you for . Blocking an attack launches a projectile towards the attacker dealing  damage, pushing the target towards you and inflicting . Recast during the effect to launch a chaos projectile.|width=5px}}


In [https://blog.stunlock.com/v-rising-1-0-patch-notes/ Update 1.0] it was finally reworked into its current iteration.

In the Early Access version of V Rising Raging Tempest originally belonged to the Illusion Magic School under the name . It had the following effect:
{{Quote|Dash forward and bounce between nearby enemies striking them for a total of  magic damage split across targets within the area over .  target hit by  for . Afterward, dash towards your aim direction. Recast to end this effect early.|width=5px}}


It was reworked into its current iteration and moved to the Storm Magic School with the Secrets of Gloomrot update on May 17th, 2023.

In the Early Access version of V Rising Volatile Arachnid was a multi-charge ultimate spell with 4 charges that had to be used within a 6.5s recast time. Each spider also left behind a toxic fume AoE lasting 8s.
It had the following effect:
{{Quote|Summon spiderlings that chase down your enemy and explode when nearby dealing  magic damage. Spawns a toxic fume that deals  magic damage every  while slowing enemies by -25%. Can be recast up to  times.|width=5px}}

After the Secrets of Gloomrot expansion on May 17th, 2023 it was reworked, with its toxic fume AoE removed. It had the following effect:
{{Quote|Summon spiderlings that chase down your enemy and explode when nearby dealing 130% magic damage and inflicting . Deals  damage and inflicts a  fading snare at the summoning location.|width=5px}}

It was finally reworked again in Update 1.0 to its current version as a single cast spell.

In the Early Access version of V Rising, Phantom Aegis belonged to the Blood Magic School under the name . It had a cooldown of  and the following effect:
{{Quote|Apply a shield to target ally or self that shields the target for  of your spell power for . Knocks nearby enemies back when the shield is applied.|width=5px}}

In the Gloomrot update the spell was reworked into its current iteration and moved to the Illusion Magic School.

In the Early Access version of V Rising, this spell belonged to the Unholy Magic School under the name . It had a cooldown of ,  charges and the following effect:
{{Quote|Summon a mosquito that chases an enemy and explodes after . Deals  magic damage in an area and inflict Amplify that increases damage taken by  for .|width=5px}}

In the Gloomrot expansion the spell was then reworked and moved to the Illusion Magic School.
It had a cooldown of ,  charge and the following effect:
{{Quote|Summon a spectral mosquito at target location that explodes after  dealing  magic damage and inflicting  and fearing enemies for up to . Grants  on hit for each enemy hit.|width=5px}}


In [https://blog.stunlock.com/v-rising-1-0-patch-notes/ Update 1.0] it was reworked into its current iteration, no longer chasing enemies, but instead remaining in place and attracting enemy aggro.

As mentioned, Wisp Dance was initially a basic spell prior to being reworked with the release of V Rising's first expansion, Secrets of Gloomrot, on May 17th, 2023.
It had a cooldown of  and the following effect:
{{Quote|Summons three wisps that circle around you, dealing  magic damage to enemies. Recast to launch all three wisps as projectiles dealing  magic damage and weakening the target reducing the damage output by  for . The recast has cast time of .|width=5px}}

